<ArticleLayout
  title="Mattress Sizes Australia: Room, Base and Buying Guide"
  seoTitle="Mattress Sizes Australia: Dimensions and Room Guide"
  description="Compare Australian mattress sizes, the complete bed footprint, room and base checks, delivery access, mattress height and trial conditions."
  category="Bedroom"
  date="Published July 2026"
  datePublished="2026-07-23"
  readingTime="7 minute read"
  faqs={faqs}
  showAffiliateDisclosure={false}
  image="/images/guides/bedroom-storage-clear-walkway.webp"
  imageAlt="A compact bedroom showing the bed footprint, open wardrobe and clear walking space beside the bed"
  imagePosition="60% 68%"
>
  <p>
    A larger mattress changes more than the sleeping surface. It changes the bed frame footprint,
    the space beside the bed, the cost of sheets and protectors, and whether the mattress can turn
    through the hallway. Mattress height can also make an existing bedside table or fitted sheet
    unsuitable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Start with the room and base, then compare comfort and construction. Australian Home Collective
    has not slept on or tested mattresses for this guide, so it does not rank brands or promise that
    one construction will feel comfortable for every person.
  </p>

  <h2>Australian size labels use manufacturer-specific dimensions</h2>
  <p>
    Names such as single, queen and king are familiar market labels, not one legally universal set
    of dimensions. The{" "}
    <a href="https://www.sealy.com.au/mattress-sizes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sealy Australia mattress-size guide</a>{" "}
    and{" "}
    <a href="https://www.sleepmaker.com.au/pages/mattress-size-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SleepMaker Australia mattress-size guide</a>{" "}
    publish different dimensions for several labels. Sealy also states a manufacturing tolerance of
    plus or minus 15 mm for its handmade mattresses, while SleepMaker says its mattresses may vary
    1–2 cm from its indicative guide. These are manufacturer statements about their own products,
    not a national legal standard.
  </p>
  <p class="table-hint">Swipe sideways to compare the full table.</p>
  <div class="comparison-wrap">
    <table class="comparison-table">
      <caption>Published Australian manufacturer examples, not universal dimensions</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Size</th>
          <th scope="col">Sealy example (W × L)</th>
          <th scope="col">SleepMaker example (W × L)</th>
          <th scope="col">Buyer action</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Single</td>
          <td>91.5 × 190 cm</td>
          <td>92 × 188 cm</td>
          <td>Measure the exact mattress, base and any enclosing rails.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Single XL</td>
          <td>91.5 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>92 × 203 cm (listed as Long Single)</td>
          <td>Check both the label and dimensions because naming also varies.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>King single</td>
          <td>105.5 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>107 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>Confirm frame, protector and sheet fit against the exact product.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Double</td>
          <td>138.5 × 190 cm</td>
          <td>137 × 188 cm</td>
          <td>Do not transfer dimensions from one maker's chart to another.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Queen</td>
          <td>152.5 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>153 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>Check internal frame size as well as the outside footprint.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>King</td>
          <td>183.5 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>183 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>Add the complete frame before judging room clearance.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Super king</td>
          <td>203 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>203 × 203 cm</td>
          <td>Still confirm the exact product and stated tolerance.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Measure the bed frame, not only the mattress</h2>
  <p>
    A frame with rails, upholstery or a broad bedhead can be wider and longer than its mattress.
    Record the maximum outside dimensions. Mark that rectangle on the floor and include the depth
    of any leaning bedhead or drawers that extend from the sides.
  </p>
  <p>
    Open the bedroom door, wardrobe and bedside drawers. Walk the route used at night and when making
    the bed. If the room needs a cot, mobility aid, laundry basket or access from both sides, include
    it in the test rather than treating empty floor as spare space.
  </p>

  <h2>Treat firmness labels as maker-specific descriptions</h2>
  <p>
    Do not assume that medium or a number out of ten is directly comparable across brands unless
    both publish a common method. Ask each maker how its label is defined within that range and test
    the exact mattress on the permitted base where possible.
  </p>
  <p>
    Try the normal sleeping position for more than a few minutes where possible. For a mattress bought online,
    read the complete trial conditions before opening the package and keep the mattress protected as
    required. A trial is valuable only when the household can comply with its minimum period, pickup
    area and return process.
  </p>

  <h2>The base can change support and warranty eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    Check whether the manufacturer permits solid platforms, slats or adjustable bases. The{" "}
    <a href="https://afterpurchase.sleepmaker.com.au/hc/en-us/articles/212535668-What-to-expect-from-your-sleep-set" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SleepMaker after-purchase guidance</a>{" "}
    specifies slats no more than 8 cm apart and a centre support rail for its mattresses, and warns
    that an unsuitable base may affect the mattress and warranty. That measurement is SleepMaker's
    instruction, not a universal rule; use the requirements for the exact mattress.
  </p>
  <p>
    Measure the internal frame rather than relying on its size label. Check whether edge rails sit
    above the support surface and whether the mattress can expand without being pinched. A heavy
    hybrid also needs a frame and floor suited to its total loaded weight.
  </p>

  <h2>Mattress height changes the complete bed</h2>
  <p>
    Add mattress height to the top of the base. Sit on the resulting height and check whether both
    feet reach the floor comfortably and whether the bedside surface remains reachable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deep mattresses need fitted sheets and protectors with enough pocket depth. Allow extra fabric
    for toppers. Check that bedding will not pull tight at the corners or slip off when an adjustable
    base moves.
  </p>

  <h2>Delivery involves weight, turns and expansion space</h2>
  <p>
    A mattress delivered in a box still has weight and a large final size. Check the box dimensions,
    stair turns, lift limits and who will move it into position. Unroll it on the intended base if the
    instructions allow, because a fully expanded king mattress is much harder to turn in a small room.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read the opening window, expansion guidance and advice about sleeping on it. Keep children and
    pets clear while packaging releases. Arrange old mattress removal before delivery where the home
    cannot safely store both.
  </p>

  <h2>Look beyond comfort on the first night</h2>
  <p>
    A short showroom trial cannot show how a mattress will retain its shape. Look for clearly
    described independent durability testing where it is available, then read the warranty's
    indentation limits, support requirements and care instructions.
  </p>
  <ul class="feature-list">
    <li>Read how the warranty defines a measurable indentation.</li>
    <li>Check rotation and care instructions.</li>
    <li>Confirm whether the cover can be removed or only spot cleaned.</li>
    <li>Ask how firmness parts, covers and other components are replaced.</li>
    <li>Check whether durability evidence describes the method and length of testing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>A practical buying checklist</h2>
  <ul class="feature-list">
    <li>Confirm the exact mattress width, length and height.</li>
    <li>Mark the complete bed frame footprint on the floor.</li>
    <li>Open doors and drawers and walk the normal routes.</li>
    <li>Check the base type, slat gaps, support and weight capacity.</li>
    <li>Measure the delivery box and every turn to the bedroom.</li>
    <li>Read the complete trial, return and pickup terms.</li>
    <li>Check sheet and protector pocket depth.</li>
    <li>Check durability evidence and warranty indentation terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <RelatedGuidesBlock guides={relatedGuides} />
</ArticleLayout>
